ideo","src","poster","/GameMap/assets/media/demos/recording-wonderworld-cathedral.webp","aspectRatio",2.5945945945945947,"mobile","previewSrc","Preview description","Official WonderWorld split-screen recording showing a cathedral first-person view and an expanding 3D scene overview","alt","Recording type","Original project recording","role","provenance","Track","World models","track","metadata","Related project",[91],"resourceId",{"_49":92,"_26":93},"WonderWorld","/resources/wonderworld/","What this recording shows","An accelerated recording of interactive scene generation, not a complete playable game or a browser model inference session. The separate project-page viewer renders pregenerated worlds; it was not loaded in this check.","limitations","Demo category","Scene generation","demoType","lead","world","scenes","source-recording","recordingId","wonderworld","resource:wonderworld","resource","Builds an explorable, expandable explicit 3D scene from a single image.","/resources/",{"_20":105,"_178":92,"_176":101,"_47":179,"_177":108,"_172":171,"_26":169,"_57":180,"_155":181,"_150":182,"_146":183,"_140":184,"_137":136},[113,114,115,116,117,118,119,120,121,122,123,124,125,126],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_47":22,"_51":92,"_53":178,"_55":-7},{"_47":100,"_51":108,"_53":177,"_55":-7},{"_47":48,"_49":175,"_51":85,"_53":176,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_49":173,"_51":174,"_53":47,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_49":170,"_51":171,"_53":172,"_55":56},{"_47":57,"_49":166,"_59":167,"_53":26,"_55":-7},{"_47":57,"_49":161,"_59":162,"_53":57,"_55":-7},{"_47":141,"_49":153,"_143":144,"_59":154,"_53":155,"_55":-7},{"_47":141,"_49":148,"_143":144,"_59":149,"_53":150,"_55":-7},{"_47":141,"_49":142,"_143":144,"_59":145,"_53":146,"_55":-7},{"_47":48,"_49":138,"_51":139,"_53":140,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_49":135,"_51":136,"_53":137,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_53":132,"_49":133,"_51":134},{"_47":57,"_53":127,"_49":128,"_59":129},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[130],{"_49":131,"_26":63},"Stanford University","identity","Identity & attribution","The author page lists equal-contribution first authors Hong-Xing (Koven) Yu and Haoyi Duan at Stanford University, with MIT also represented. Select Stanford. The logo is the official touch icon linked by https://identity.stanford.edu/.","Source reviewed","2026-10-18","verified","Year","2024","year","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[147,85],"dimensions","3D","Development stages",[151,152,85],"stages","Assets & animation","Engines & scenes","Topics",[156,157,158,159,160],"tags","scene-generation","explicit-3d","Gaussian-surfels","camera-control","CVPR-2025","Further reading",[163],{"_49":164,"_26":165},"Project","https://kovenyu.com/WonderWorld/","Project source",[168],{"_49":166,"_26":169},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.09394","Why it belongs here","Interactive 3D Scene Generation from a Single Image uses Fast Layered Gaussian Surfels and guided depth diffusion to connect new scenes as the camera moves and prompts change. It provides explicit spatial representation and real-time rendering, primarily addressing geometry and appearance. Interactive gameplay, physics, and persistent dynamic state still require separate implementation.","detail","Resource type","Paper","Category","category","summary","name","paper",[188],[156,157,158,159,160],[186,187,101],[185,101],2024,"3d","assets","scene",{"_49":164,"_26":165},{"_190":191},"documents",{"_192":193,"_194":195},"en",[197,201,202,203,200,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220,221,222,223,224,225,226,227,228,229,230,231,232,233,234,235,199,236,198,237,238,239,240,241,242,243,244,245,246,247,248,249,250,251,252,253,254],"zh",[196,197,198,199,200],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation